// REAL dev-foundation flight on node-2 (not part of the unit suite; DEV ONLY; no paid calls). The owner's end-to-end
// "Cyrus builds a mod on a vanilla FOUNDATION" demo, with a hand-written ModSpec in place of the model:
//   1. catalog_search / catalog_get exactly as the build model calls them (vanilla reference rows + foundation rows)
//   2. the pick goes into a ModSpec slot { source: "imported", foundationRef: "vf:<sha256>" } (validated)
//   3. the slot is resolved against the dev store, the base becomes a studio doc stamped game-derived, and a
//      deterministic "Cyrus edit" retextures it (ember recolour + glow tip)
//   4. the resource pack is built: the unchanged base copy is LEFT OUT (delta-only), the retexture ships
//   5. the vanilla validators run over the pack; then a real Test Flight boots Paper 26.1.2 with the TfItemModel
//      fixture plugin through the gate's own flyOne(), the vanilla summary riding on the flight record
